At the exact moment when the snowflake's branching arms, crystalline ridges, hexagonal facets, and frosted textures naturally match the mountain ranges, frozen lakes, icy valleys, and radial layout of @Image 2, transition seamlessly into the aerial view of the frozen kingdom. Continue the same uninterrupted forward movement toward the magnificent ice citadel at the center as crystalline facets become frozen lakes, delicate frost becomes snow-covered forests, microscopic ice ridges become towering mountain chains, and the central hexagon transforms into the heart of the kingdom. Preserve the feeling that the viewer has never left the same crystalline structure—only its scale has expanded from a single snowflake to an entire frozen world.

No tearing, black frames, hard cuts, visible morphing, obvious VFX, or compositing seams. Keep the transformation completely photorealistic, elegant, and physically believable—as though the microscopic architecture of a snowflake naturally unfolds into a colossal frozen kingdom. Preserve the continuity of crystalline branches becoming mountain ridges, ice facets becoming frozen lakes, frost particles becoming drifting snowfall, and sparkling highlights becoming sunlight glinting across glaciers and ice palaces. Maintain identical cool blue lighting, atmospheric continuity, and one continuous cinematic camera push with no visible edit.

